11.0.0 — the app asks for Inter-App Audio, other makers' plugins load and play more reliably, and a Launchpad never flashes past three a second

New since 10087, built by the Echoel Studio run; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- The app now asks iOS for Inter-App Audio (F44). With it, instruments of other makers may appear
  in Audio Unit Instrument on a track's Sound page; whether they do only a device shows.
- A plugin of another maker whose busses take one channel plays through the host, and a unit
  that refuses stereo when it allocates is tried in mono.
- Its main busses are switched on and set after its saved settings, so an effect hears its input.
- A unit that does not start within 15 seconds says so instead of loading for ever.
- Reload Plugin on its page loads a unit again that failed, stopped too often or refuses audio,
  and the page says how many audio blocks it refused. Reloading one plugin keeps what the status
  line says about the others.
- A plugin that hands back less audio than a block asked for no longer plays stray sound: an
  instrument adds nothing for that block, an effect lets the sound through as it was, and the
  page counts the block as refused.
- A plugin's page says when its settings did not reach the song.
- A unit that builds a new parameter tree (a mode, a preset) is followed by automation and its page.
- Channel pressure, poly pressure and program change from your controller reach a plugin
  instrument; under a key lock, poly pressure follows the note its key plays.
- A plugin installed while the app runs appears in the list without an older scan hiding it.
- A Launchpad's waiting and playing pads flash and pulse only while the clock it follows stays at
  180 BPM or below; above that they stay steady, in colour. After our clock stops, the device keeps
  the tempo it heard last, so the pads stay steady until a slower clock of ours has run three
  seconds, also after a reconnect or a relaunch.
- A note sent through MPE Out is never left hanging when the app falls behind: every note ends.
- A media-browser preview that ends, and a stopped song with an arpeggiator, no longer free or
  allocate memory on the audio thread.

Previous: 10087. A green commit that changes this file uploads build 10000 + run number. A test
list, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

One ask, as for 10083 to 10087. Start a screen recording, open the app, and try to make sixteen
bars in two to five minutes: a beat, a bass line or a chord, then Play. No list and no protocol; stop wherever
it stops being possible or pleasant. The recording is the answer. What gets in the way in it is
the next work, in the order it happened. Before you stop, open Audio Unit Instrument on a track's
Sound page once, so the recording shows whether other makers' instruments are listed (F44).

The five checks of 10079 stay open and unchanged and rest until that recording exists.
